  "id": "passive-dead-hang",
  "name": "Passive Dead Hang",
  "definition": "A strict bilateral timed hang from a horizontal pull-up bar using a shoulder-width closed pronated grip, unsupported feet, fully extended elbows, and no deliberate swing. The athlete maintains a secure grip while allowing the shoulders to rise naturally toward the ears and does not deliberately depress or cycle the shoulder blades. The only resisted action is hand.fingerExtension; the shoulder position is a held fixture, not an authored scapular action. Army and CrossFit standards directly establish the grip, straight-arm suspension, and passive shoulder boundary. Grip and support-chain roles are conservative anatomy-and-mechanics inferences rather than exact bar-hang rankings, and the involvement roster is not an exhaustive tissue-load atlas. Active Dead Hang, Scapular Pull-Up, flexed-arm holds, Pull-Ups, climbing-edge hangs, weighted hangs, swinging, and foot-assisted hangs remain outside this contract.",
